COPY public.cs_erp_context_index (id, entity_type, entity_id, context_text, embedding, created_at) FROM stdin;
\.
COPY public.cs_erp_features (id, module_id, name, description, ai_automated, status) FROM stdin;
FEAT-002-1-001	MOD-002	Cloud Native Deployment	Kubernetes-based container orchestration with multi-region AWS/Azure deployment, auto-scaling for shipping workload peaks, and infrastructure-as-code for reproducible ERP environments	f	pending
FEAT-002-1-002	MOD-002	Identity & Access Management	Role-based access control with SSO integration, multi-factor authentication, and shipping industry DOA (Delegation of Authority) hierarchy for approval workflows across Qatar, Dubai, KSA, and India entities	f	pending
FEAT-002-1-003	MOD-002	Data Encryption & Key Management	End-to-end data encryption with AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit, HSM-backed key management, automated key rotation, and field-level encryption for sensitive shipping documents and financial data	f	pending
FEAT-002-1-004	MOD-002	Audit Trail & Compliance Logging	Comprehensive immutable audit trail capturing all user actions, AI agent decisions, system events, and data changes across the shipping ERP with SOC2/ISO 27001 compliance reporting and maritime regulatory evidence	t	pending
FEAT-001-1-001	MOD-001	Multi-Agent Orchestration Engine	Core orchestration layer that manages lifecycle, communication, coordination, and fault tolerance of all AI agents across the container shipping ERP platform, enabling parallel agent execution with dependency-aware task scheduling	t	pending
FEAT-001-1-002	MOD-001	Document Intelligence Agent	AI-powered document processing agent specialized for maritime shipping documents including Bills of Lading, cargo manifests, charter party agreements, and dangerous goods declarations with OCR, entity extraction, validation, and classification capabilities	t	pending
FEAT-002-2-001	MOD-002	API Gateway & Service Mesh	Centralized API gateway with rate limiting, authentication enforcement, intelligent routing, circuit breakers, and service discovery for all container shipping microservices	t	pending
FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	Disaster Recovery & Business Continuity	Comprehensive disaster recovery with defined RTO/RPO targets, multi-region failover, automated backups, and operational runbooks ensuring continuous container shipping operations	t	pending
FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	Monitoring Alerting & Observability	Comprehensive observability stack with APM, centralized log aggregation, distributed tracing, and SLA dashboards providing full visibility into container shipping ERP operations	t	pending
FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	Data Residency & Sovereignty	Comprehensive data residency controls ensuring compliance with Qatar PDPL, UAE DPL, KSA PDPL, and India DPDPA data protection laws with cross-border transfer controls for container shipping operations	t	pending
FEAT-002-3-001	MOD-002	Network Security & Zero Trust Architecture	Zero trust network model for microservices communication with DDoS protection, WAF, IDS/IPS, multi-region VPN connectivity across Qatar-Dubai-KSA-India corridors, network segmentation per service, and automated certificate management and rotation	t	pending
FEAT-002-3-002	MOD-002	Backup & Data Protection	Automated backup and data protection strategy with daily database backups, 90-day retention, point-in-time recovery, cross-region replication across Qatar-Dubai-KSA-India, backup integrity verification, and shipping data compliance retention meeting SOLAS and ISPS Code requirements	t	pending
FEAT-001-1-003	MOD-001	AI Workflow Orchestration Agent	Intelligent workflow agent that automates end-to-end container shipping processes from booking-to-bill-of-lading and voyage-to-trade-document-release, coordinating across multiple agents and systems with decision-point automation and exception handling	t	pending
FEAT-001-1-004	MOD-001	Human-in-Loop Escalation Engine	Intelligent escalation framework that enforces delegation of authority rules, manages approval queues with priority routing, and ensures critical decisions in container shipping operations receive appropriate human oversight while maintaining the 95/5 automation target	t	pending
