FEAT-060-1-002	MOD-060	HSSE Health Safety Security Environment	Integrated Health, Safety, Security, and Environment management system tailored for container shipping terminal operations at Hamad Port, Khalifa Port, Jebel Ali, and JNPT. Manages compliance with local and international HSSE standards, permits, inspections, and corrective actions across all operational entities with AI-driven anomaly detection and predictive safety analytics.	t	pending
FEAT-060-1-003	MOD-060	Near-Miss & Unsafe Act Reporting	Digital near-miss and unsafe act reporting system enabling all port personnel to quickly report safety concerns before they escalate into actual incidents. Features anonymous reporting options, AI-powered trend analysis, and gamification to encourage a proactive safety reporting culture across Hamad Port, Khalifa Port, Jebel Ali, and JNPT operations.	t	pending
FEAT-060-1-004	MOD-060	Incident Investigation & Root Cause Analysis	Structured incident investigation framework with built-in root cause analysis methodologies for container shipping operations. Supports multiple investigation techniques including 5-Why, fishbone diagrams, fault tree analysis, and barrier analysis with AI-assisted causal factor identification and cross-entity learning to prevent recurrence across all port operations.	t	pending
FEAT-060-2-001	MOD-060	P&I Club Risk Scoring AI	AI-driven risk scoring engine that continuously evaluates vessel, cargo, and voyage parameters against Protection & Indemnity club underwriting criteria. The system generates dynamic risk scores for each shipment, vessel call, and trade lane to optimize insurance premiums, flag high-risk operations for enhanced scrutiny, and provide predictive loss modeling across the Qatar/UAE/KSA/India corridor.	t	pending
FEAT-060-2-002	MOD-060	Business Continuity Plan Management	Comprehensive digital platform for creating, maintaining, testing, and activating business continuity plans across all four operating entities. The system manages BCP lifecycle from risk assessment through plan development, exercise scheduling, and activation protocols ensuring uninterrupted container shipping operations during disruptions at Hamad Port, Khalifa Port, Jebel Ali, and JNPT.	t	pending
FEAT-060-2-003	MOD-060	Emergency Response Procedure Library	Centralized digital library of emergency response procedures for all container shipping operational scenarios across Gulf and Indian subcontinent ports. The system provides instant access to step-by-step response procedures, integrates with vessel and terminal safety systems, and ensures compliance with IMO, port authority, and national emergency management regulations.	t	pending
FEAT-060-2-004	MOD-060	Risk KPI Dashboard & Board Reporting	Executive-level dashboard and automated reporting platform that presents risk key performance indicators, loss prevention metrics, and insurance portfolio performance to the board of directors and senior management. The system provides real-time risk visibility across all four entities with drill-down capabilities, automated board report generation, and regulatory risk disclosure compliance.	t	pending
FEAT-027-1-001	MOD-027	Import Customs Clearance Management	Manages the end-to-end import customs clearance lifecycle for containerized cargo arriving at Hamad Port, Khalifa Port, Jebel Ali, and JNPT. Orchestrates document preparation, duty assessment, regulatory inspections, and cargo release workflows with 95% AI automation while ensuring compliance with Qatar Customs Authority, UAE Federal Authority for Identity and Citizenship, KSA ZATCA, and Indian CBIC regulations.	t	pending
FEAT-027-1-002	MOD-027	Export Customs Filing & Submission	Manages the complete export customs declaration lifecycle for containerized cargo departing from Hamad Port, Khalifa Port, Jebel Ali, and JNPT. Automates export documentation preparation, electronic filing with customs authorities, and compliance verification against export control regulations across Qatar, UAE, KSA, and India jurisdictions.	t	pending
FEAT-027-1-003	MOD-027	Transit & Re-Export Procedures	Manages customs transit movements and re-export operations for containerized cargo moving through or temporarily stored within Qatar, UAE, KSA, and India jurisdictions. Handles transit bond management, transshipment documentation, temporary import-for-re-export procedures, and cross-border movement tracking between GCC member states.	t	pending
FEAT-027-1-004	MOD-027	Customs Duty & Tax Calculation	Provides comprehensive customs duty and tax calculation engine supporting the GCC Common External Tariff, KSA national tariff, UAE tariff schedules, Qatar duty rates, and Indian Customs Tariff. Handles multi-currency valuation, preferential duty rates under free trade agreements, anti-dumping duties, and jurisdiction-specific taxes including VAT, GST, and excise duties.	t	pending
FEAT-000-1-001	MOD-000	Authentication UI & Session Management	Complete authentication interface including login, registration, MFA enrollment, SSO integration, and secure session handling. Supports email/password, TOTP, SAML 2.0, and OAuth2.	t	pending
FEAT-000-1-002	MOD-000	Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)	Granular permission system with hierarchical roles. Supports super-admin, company-admin, module-specific roles, and custom role creation. All access decisions logged for audit.	t	pending
FEAT-000-2-001	MOD-000	Multi-Tenant Architecture	Shared database with row-level security data isolation. Company onboarding, subscription management, data residency selection (Qatar / UAE / KSA / India data centres), and tenant lifecycle management.	t	pending
FEAT-000-2-002	MOD-000	Admin Panel	Company-level admin panel for user management, role assignment, system configuration, audit logs, and module activation.	t	pending
FEAT-000-3-001	MOD-000	Dashboard Shell & Navigation	The main application shell that hosts all CS ERP modules. Responsive sidebar navigation, breadcrumbs, command palette, notification centre, and module routing with lazy loading.	t	pending
FEAT-000-3-002	MOD-000	Onboarding Flow & Company Setup	Guided setup wizard for new companies and first-time users. Data import tools, module activation sequencing, and go-live checklist.	t	pending
\.
