COPY public.cs_erp_requirements (id, feature_id, module_id, title, description, priority, ai_agent, human_touchpoint, acceptance_criteria, status) FROM stdin;
FEAT-005-2-001-R001	FEAT-005-2-001	MOD-005	Unified Customer Account Profile with Multi-Entity Hierarchy	The system must maintain a unified customer account profile that consolidates all interactions, bookings, financials, and contracts across multiple legal entities (Qatar WLL, UAE LLC, KSA CR, India Pvt Ltd). Each account must support a parent-child hierarchy allowing a single global shipper (e.g., Maersk Line) to have subsidiary accounts per jurisdiction. The profile must display all port activity across Hamad Port (QAHMD), Khalifa Port (AEKHL), Jebel Ali (AEJEA), and JNPT (INNSA) with real-time TEU volume aggregation. Arabic and English names must be stored simultaneously with RTL rendering for Arabic display contexts. The account record must include trade license numbers, CR numbers, QID/Emirates ID of authorized signatories, and VAT/GST registration numbers per entity.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-005-2-002-R010	FEAT-005-2-002	MOD-005	Quota Attainment and Payout Simulation Tool	The system must provide salespeople with a self-service simulation tool to model their projected quota attainment and resulting commission/bonus payout under different scenarios. The simulator must accept inputs for projected bookings by trade lane and container type for remaining months in the incentive period, apply the active commission plan rules including tier thresholds and accelerators, and display projected total payout in the salesperson's local currency with USD equivalent. The tool must show marginal incentive rates (additional earning per incremental TEU) at current attainment levels to motivate stretch performance. Simulations must account for clawback exposure on at-risk bookings. The tool must function offline with the last-synced commission plan parameters and reconcile upon reconnection. All simulation runs must be non-binding and clearly marked as estimates.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-005-2-004-R002	FEAT-005-2-004	MOD-005	AI-Powered Lead Scoring and Qualification Engine	The system must implement an AI-driven lead scoring model that assigns a qualification score (0-100) based on firmographic data (company size, industry, import/export volumes from public customs data), behavioral signals (website page visits, email engagement, content downloads), stated shipping requirements (volume, trade lanes, container types), geographic alignment with serviced ports (proximity to Hamad Port, Khalifa Port, Jebel Ali, JNPT hinterlands), and fit with target customer profiles per entity commercial strategy. Leads scoring above 75 must be classified as Marketing Qualified Leads (MQL) and auto-routed to the appropriate salesperson based on territory rules. The scoring model must retrain monthly on conversion outcome data. Scoring criteria weights must be configurable per entity and market segment. The system must explain score components in natural language summaries available in Arabic and English for sales team transparency.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-006-2-001-R012	FEAT-006-2-001	MOD-006	Bulk Rate Request Upload	The system must support bulk rate request submissions via CSV or Excel file upload with a predefined template containing columns for origin port UN/LOCODE, destination port UN/LOCODE, container type ISO code, commodity HS code, weight in kilograms, required ETD, INCOTERMS 2020 code, and special handling codes. The upload processor must validate each row against the master data for port codes, container types, and commodity classifications, returning a detailed error report for any invalid rows. Successfully validated rows must create individual rate requests that can be tracked independently. The bulk upload must support a maximum of 200 rows per file and must complete processing within 60 seconds.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-006-2-003-R003	FEAT-006-2-003	MOD-006	Detention and Demurrage Dispute Workflow	The system must provide a dedicated dispute workflow for detention and demurrage charges, automatically pulling the original free-time allocation, actual container gate-in/gate-out timestamps from the port community system, applicable tariff rates, and the computed charges. Customers must be able to dispute by selecting specific grounds: port congestion beyond customer control, customs hold not attributable to customer, incorrect timestamp recording, or force majeure events. The system must cross-reference the dispute grounds with port authority congestion advisories, customs clearance logs, and weather event records to auto-validate or flag the dispute for manual review. Disputes involving amounts exceeding USD 5,000 equivalent must be routed to a senior commercial manager with mandatory resolution within 10 business days.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-006-2-004-R009	FEAT-006-2-004	MOD-006	Real-Time Vessel Schedule Change Alerts	The system must send immediate notifications when a vessel schedule change affects a customer's active shipment, including vessel delay (with revised ETA), port omission, transshipment change, vessel substitution, and blank sailing. The notification must include the original schedule details, the updated schedule details, the estimated impact on the customer's cargo (revised delivery date), and recommended actions (such as rebook on alternate vessel if the delay exceeds the customer's acceptable threshold). For reefer cargo shipments, schedule changes exceeding 48 hours must trigger a high-priority alert flagged as potential cold chain risk. The system must also notify customers of weather-related advisories for ports on their shipment route sourced from maritime weather services.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-007-1-001-R015	FEAT-007-1-001	MOD-007	Tariff Search and Filtering Interface	The system must provide an advanced search interface allowing users to locate tariffs using multiple filter criteria simultaneously including origin port, destination port, container type, commodity code, effective date range, tariff status (draft, pending approval, active, expired), entity, and currency. The search interface must support Arabic text input for port names and commodity descriptions with proper RTL rendering. Search results must be sortable by any displayed column and must support pagination for large result sets. AI-powered natural language search must allow users to type queries like 'reefer rates from Hamad to JNPT next month' in either Arabic or English and return matching tariff records.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-001-1-001-R012	FEAT-001-1-001	MOD-001	Agent Metrics & Performance Dashboard	Collect and expose agent metrics including task throughput, p50/p95/p99 latency, error rates, queue depths, and resource utilization via Prometheus-compatible endpoints with pre-built Grafana dashboard templates	must_have			[]	pending
