FEAT-026-2-001-R009	FEAT-026-2-001	MOD-026	Delivery SLA Monitoring and Penalty Calculation	The system must track delivery performance against configurable Service Level Agreements defined per customer contract, trade lane, and entity. SLA metrics shall include on-time delivery percentage (target configurable, default 95%), average delivery lead time from ICD gate-out to consignee ePOD, and first-attempt delivery success rate. When SLA thresholds are breached, the system must automatically calculate penalty amounts per the contract terms, generate credit notes in the appropriate currency (QAR/AED/SAR/INR), and notify the account manager via email and in-app alert. SLA dashboards must display Hijri and Gregorian date ranges with drill-down capability to individual delivery orders.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R009	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL implement message queue (Kafka/RabbitMQ) replication across regions so that unprocessed booking events, container status updates, and EDI messages are not lost during regional failover	System SHALL implement message queue (Kafka/RabbitMQ) replication across regions so that unprocessed booking events, container status updates, and EDI messages are not lost during regional failover	must_have			"Message queue mirrors all topics to secondary region with lag under 10 seconds; after failover, secondary region consumers process all mirrored messages; no booking events or EDI messages are lost; message ordering is preserved per partition/queue"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R010	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL conduct full disaster recovery drills semi-annually, simulating complete primary region loss and measuring actual RTO/RPO against targets for all shipping services	System SHALL conduct full disaster recovery drills semi-annually, simulating complete primary region loss and measuring actual RTO/RPO against targets for all shipping services	must_have			"DR drill simulates complete primary region unavailability; all critical services failover and process test bookings successfully; actual RTO and RPO are measured and documented; gaps between target and actual are tracked as action items; drill report is submitted to management within 5 business days"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R011	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL maintain a warm standby environment in the secondary region with pre-provisioned compute capacity at 50% of primary, auto-scaling to 100% upon failover activation	System SHALL maintain a warm standby environment in the secondary region with pre-provisioned compute capacity at 50% of primary, auto-scaling to 100% upon failover activation	should_have			"Secondary region runs at 50% compute capacity during normal operations; failover trigger initiates auto-scaling to 100% capacity within 10 minutes; scaled environment handles full production booking and tracking load; cost of warm standby is tracked and reported monthly"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R012	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL implement split-brain prevention for multi-region database clusters using quorum-based consensus, ensuring only one region accepts write operations for booking and BL data at any time	System SHALL implement split-brain prevention for multi-region database clusters using quorum-based consensus, ensuring only one region accepts write operations for booking and BL data at any time	must_have			"Network partition between regions results in only one region accepting writes; split-brain scenario is detected within 10 seconds; conflicting writes are prevented; resolution procedure restores cluster consistency; split-brain event triggers P1 alert with automated diagnostics"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R013	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL provide a DR status dashboard showing real-time replication lag, backup freshness, secondary region health, and last successful DR drill date for all shipping services	System SHALL provide a DR status dashboard showing real-time replication lag, backup freshness, secondary region health, and last successful DR drill date for all shipping services	should_have			"Dashboard displays replication lag per service in seconds; backup age is shown with red/amber/green indicators; secondary region health checks update every 30 seconds; last DR drill date and result are prominently displayed; dashboard is accessible to ops and management roles"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R014	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL implement automated chaos engineering tests monthly, randomly terminating shipping service instances and validating self-healing recovery within defined RTO thresholds	System SHALL implement automated chaos engineering tests monthly, randomly terminating shipping service instances and validating self-healing recovery within defined RTO thresholds	should_have			"Monthly chaos test terminates random service instances during business hours; affected services self-heal within RTO; booking and tracking endpoints return to normal within 15 minutes; chaos test results are documented with recovery timeline; tests run in production with safeguards"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R015	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL maintain an offline-capable mode for port terminal operations, queuing booking confirmations and container gate-in/gate-out events locally and synchronizing when connectivity is restored	System SHALL maintain an offline-capable mode for port terminal operations, queuing booking confirmations and container gate-in/gate-out events locally and synchronizing when connectivity is restored	should_have			"Port terminal client continues accepting gate-in/gate-out events during connectivity loss; events are queued locally with timestamps; upon reconnection, queued events sync to central system with conflict detection; sync completes within 10 minutes for up to 5000 queued events"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R016	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL implement point-in-time recovery (PITR) for all shipping databases, enabling restoration to any second within the last 35 days to recover from data corruption or erroneous bulk operations	System SHALL implement point-in-time recovery (PITR) for all shipping databases, enabling restoration to any second within the last 35 days to recover from data corruption or erroneous bulk operations	must_have			"PITR restore to arbitrary timestamp within 35-day window completes within 4 hours for full database; restored data matches expected state at target timestamp; PITR is tested quarterly as part of backup validation; WAL/binlog retention supports 35-day window"	pending
FEAT-002-2-002-R017	FEAT-002-2-002	MOD-002	System SHALL implement automated SSL/TLS certificate disaster recovery, ensuring replacement certificates for all shipping API endpoints are issued within 1 hour if primary certificate authority becomes compromised	System SHALL implement automated SSL/TLS certificate disaster recovery, ensuring replacement certificates for all shipping API endpoints are issued within 1 hour if primary certificate authority becomes compromised	should_have			"Backup CA is pre-configured and tested quarterly; emergency certificate reissuance procedure completes within 1 hour; all shipping API endpoints serve valid certificates after switch; certificate pinning clients receive advance notification via pre-established channel"	pending
FEAT-027-2-001-R005	FEAT-027-2-001	MOD-027	AEO Audit Trail and Evidence Repository	The system must maintain an immutable audit trail of all AEO-related activities including self-assessments completed, corrective actions taken, document submissions to customs authorities, and communication logs with AEO program offices. Each audit entry shall be timestamped in UTC with local time zone conversion for Doha (AST), Dubai/Abu Dhabi (GST), Riyadh (AST), and Mumbai (IST). The evidence repository must store supporting documents such as security certifications, financial statements, customs compliance reports, and internal audit findings with version control. All documents must be searchable in both Arabic and English, with metadata tagging for quick retrieval during customs authority inspections or annual AEO re-validation audits.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R001	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL deploy APM agents on all shipping microservices capturing transaction response times, throughput, and error rates with per-endpoint granularity for booking, tracking, BL, and customs services	System SHALL deploy APM agents on all shipping microservices capturing transaction response times, throughput, and error rates with per-endpoint granularity for booking, tracking, BL, and customs services	must_have			"APM dashboard shows p50, p95, p99 response times per endpoint; throughput is displayed as requests/second; error rate percentage is calculated per 5-minute window; APM overhead does not exceed 3% CPU and 50MB memory per service instance"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R002	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL aggregate logs from all shipping services into a centralized log store with structured JSON format, supporting search and filtering by correlation ID, shipment reference, container number, and BL number	System SHALL aggregate logs from all shipping services into a centralized log store with structured JSON format, supporting search and filtering by correlation ID, shipment reference, container number, and BL number	must_have			"All service logs are ingested within 30 seconds of emission; logs are searchable by correlation-id, shipment-ref, container-number, and bl-number fields; log retention is 90 days for hot storage and 1 year for cold archive; search query returns results within 5 seconds for last 24 hours"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R003	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL implement distributed tracing across all service-to-service calls, providing end-to-end trace visualization for complete shipment lifecycle from booking creation through BL surrender	System SHALL implement distributed tracing across all service-to-service calls, providing end-to-end trace visualization for complete shipment lifecycle from booking creation through BL surrender	must_have			"Single trace captures entire booking-to-BL workflow across booking-service, documentation-service, customs-service, and tracking-service; trace waterfall view shows timing for each span; traces are retained for 30 days; trace search by shipment reference returns results within 3 seconds"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R004	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL provide SLA dashboards showing real-time and historical uptime percentages per shipping service, with targets of 99.95% for booking and tracking, and 99.9% for documentation and reporting services	System SHALL provide SLA dashboards showing real-time and historical uptime percentages per shipping service, with targets of 99.95% for booking and tracking, and 99.9% for documentation and reporting services	must_have			"Dashboard displays current month uptime percentage per service; historical view shows last 12 months; SLA breach is highlighted in red when uptime drops below target; dashboard auto-refreshes every 60 seconds; uptime calculation excludes planned maintenance windows"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R005	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL trigger PagerDuty alerts within 60 seconds when booking-service error rate exceeds 1% or response time p95 exceeds 2 seconds, with escalation to on-call shipping operations manager after 15 minutes unacknowledged	System SHALL trigger PagerDuty alerts within 60 seconds when booking-service error rate exceeds 1% or response time p95 exceeds 2 seconds, with escalation to on-call shipping operations manager after 15 minutes unacknowledged	must_have			"Error rate exceeding 1% triggers alert within 60 seconds; p95 latency exceeding 2 seconds triggers alert within 60 seconds; unacknowledged alert escalates after 15 minutes; alert includes service name, current metrics, and runbook link; alert de-duplicates within 5-minute window"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R006	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL monitor database query performance, alerting when any shipping database query exceeds 500ms execution time or when connection pool utilization exceeds 80% for booking or BL databases	System SHALL monitor database query performance, alerting when any shipping database query exceeds 500ms execution time or when connection pool utilization exceeds 80% for booking or BL databases	must_have			"Slow query log captures all queries exceeding 500ms with full SQL and execution plan; connection pool utilization alert fires at 80% threshold; dashboard shows top 10 slowest queries over last hour; alert includes database name, query fingerprint, and execution time"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R007	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL implement synthetic monitoring that executes end-to-end booking creation and tracking lookup test transactions every 5 minutes from each deployment region, alerting on failure	System SHALL implement synthetic monitoring that executes end-to-end booking creation and tracking lookup test transactions every 5 minutes from each deployment region, alerting on failure	must_have			"Synthetic booking test runs every 5 minutes from Middle East and South Asia regions; test creates booking, verifies confirmation, queries tracking status; failure triggers alert within 1 minute; synthetic transaction results are excluded from production metrics; uptime is calculated from synthetic checks"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R008	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL capture and display infrastructure metrics including CPU, memory, disk I/O, and network throughput for all Kubernetes pods running shipping services with 15-second granularity	System SHALL capture and display infrastructure metrics including CPU, memory, disk I/O, and network throughput for all Kubernetes pods running shipping services with 15-second granularity	must_have			"Metrics are collected every 15 seconds for all pods; dashboard shows CPU and memory utilization per pod and per service aggregate; disk I/O and network throughput are displayed for database pods; metrics retention is 90 days at 15-second resolution and 1 year at 5-minute resolution"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R009	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL implement anomaly detection on booking volume patterns, alerting when hourly booking count deviates more than 3 standard deviations from the rolling 4-week same-day-of-week average	System SHALL implement anomaly detection on booking volume patterns, alerting when hourly booking count deviates more than 3 standard deviations from the rolling 4-week same-day-of-week average	should_have			"Anomaly detection runs hourly comparing current booking volume to 4-week historical average for same day and hour; deviation beyond 3 sigma triggers alert; both unusually high (possible bot attack) and unusually low (possible outage) deviations are detected; alert includes current count, expected range, and deviation magnitude"	pending
FEAT-026-2-001-R010	FEAT-026-2-001	MOD-026	Return and Empty Container Pickup Coordination	The system must manage the reverse logistics of empty container pickup from consignee premises after destuffing. Empty pickup orders must be linked to the original delivery order and Bill of Lading. The system must enforce container detention and demurrage free-time rules per the shipping line's tariff, calculating charges in the billing currency when free time is exceeded. Pickup scheduling must coordinate with the shipping line's empty depot or container yard availability. The system must track empty container condition at pickup (food-grade clean, damaged, PTI-passed for reefers) and route damaged containers to designated repair depots. Multi-entity scenarios where a container delivered by the UAE entity is returned through a KSA depot must be handled via inter-entity transfer workflows.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-047-2-001-R004	FEAT-047-2-001	MOD-047	Port-Wise Performance Breakdown	The system must provide a port-wise performance breakdown view showing each agent's metrics segmented by origin and destination ports including Hamad Port (QAHMD), Khalifa Port (AEKHL), Jebel Ali (AEJEA), JNPT (INNHV), and any other configured ports in the network. Metrics per port must include TEU count by container type (20GP, 40GP, 40HC, 20RF, 40RF), average transit time adherence, demurrage and detention incidents caused by agent delays, and customs clearance success rate. The breakdown must support drill-down from port level to individual shipment level with full audit trail.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R011	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL implement log-based alerting for security events including failed authentication attempts exceeding 10 per minute per IP, unauthorized API access attempts, and privilege escalation patterns	System SHALL implement log-based alerting for security events including failed authentication attempts exceeding 10 per minute per IP, unauthorized API access attempts, and privilege escalation patterns	must_have			"Alert triggers when single IP generates more than 10 failed auth attempts in 60 seconds; unauthorized scope access generates immediate alert; privilege escalation patterns (e.g., role change + immediate admin API call) are detected; security alerts route to dedicated security team channel"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R012	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL implement Kafka/message queue monitoring tracking consumer lag per topic, alerting when booking-events or container-status-updates topic lag exceeds 10,000 messages or 5 minutes processing delay	System SHALL implement Kafka/message queue monitoring tracking consumer lag per topic, alerting when booking-events or container-status-updates topic lag exceeds 10,000 messages or 5 minutes processing delay	must_have			"Consumer lag is displayed per topic and consumer group; alert fires when booking-events lag exceeds 10,000 messages; alert fires when lag time exceeds 5 minutes; dashboard shows lag trend over last 24 hours; alert includes topic name, current lag, and consumer group"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R013	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL provide a network topology visualization showing service-to-service communication patterns, request volumes, and error rates between all shipping microservices in real time	System SHALL provide a network topology visualization showing service-to-service communication patterns, request volumes, and error rates between all shipping microservices in real time	should_have			"Topology map displays all services as nodes with edges showing communication; edge thickness reflects request volume; edge color indicates error rate (green <1%, amber 1-5%, red >5%); visualization updates every 30 seconds; clicking edge shows detailed metrics between two services"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R014	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL implement cost monitoring dashboards tracking cloud infrastructure spend per shipping service, per region, and per resource type with daily granularity and monthly budget alerts	System SHALL implement cost monitoring dashboards tracking cloud infrastructure spend per shipping service, per region, and per resource type with daily granularity and monthly budget alerts	should_have			"Dashboard shows daily spend per service and per region; budget threshold alerts fire at 80% and 100% of monthly budget; cost anomaly detection flags daily spend exceeding 150% of 30-day average; cost data is available within 24 hours of incurrence"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R016	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL implement on-call rotation management integrated with alerting, automatically routing shipping operations alerts to current on-call engineer with timezone-aware scheduling for Gulf and South Asian operations	System SHALL implement on-call rotation management integrated with alerting, automatically routing shipping operations alerts to current on-call engineer with timezone-aware scheduling for Gulf and South Asian operations	should_have			"On-call schedule supports weekly rotation with timezone awareness for Gulf (GMT+3/+4) and South Asian (GMT+5:30) teams; alerts route to current on-call engineer; schedule overrides are supported for holidays and leave; handoff notifications are sent 1 hour before rotation change"	pending
FEAT-002-2-003-R017	FEAT-002-2-003	MOD-002	System SHALL retain all observability data (metrics, logs, traces) with immutable audit trail for 1 year to support maritime regulatory compliance investigations and dispute resolution for shipping claims	System SHALL retain all observability data (metrics, logs, traces) with immutable audit trail for 1 year to support maritime regulatory compliance investigations and dispute resolution for shipping claims	must_have			"Metrics, logs, and traces are stored immutably for 1 year; data cannot be modified or deleted within retention period; audit queries for specific shipment references return all associated observability data; storage tiering moves data older than 90 days to cold storage while maintaining query capability within 30 seconds"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R001	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL store all personal data of Qatar-based shippers, consignees, and customs brokers exclusively within Qatar-region data centers in compliance with Qatar Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL) Article 13	System SHALL store all personal data of Qatar-based shippers, consignees, and customs brokers exclusively within Qatar-region data centers in compliance with Qatar Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL) Article 13	must_have			"User records with Qatar nationality or Qatar-registered business addresses are stored in Qatar-region database; database audit confirms no Qatar personal data exists in non-Qatar regions; data residency check runs daily and flags violations; compliance report is generated monthly"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R002	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL enforce UAE data localization requirements by storing all shipping transaction data involving UAE free zone operations (JAFZA, DAFZA, KIZAD) within UAE-region infrastructure	System SHALL enforce UAE data localization requirements by storing all shipping transaction data involving UAE free zone operations (JAFZA, DAFZA, KIZAD) within UAE-region infrastructure	must_have			"Bookings with UAE free zone origin or destination have transaction data stored in UAE region; BL data for UAE port operations resides in UAE; audit query confirms zero UAE free zone transaction records in non-UAE regions; data includes customs declarations, gate-in/out records, and container tracking for UAE ports"	pending
FEAT-026-2-001-R011	FEAT-026-2-001	MOD-026	Hazardous Cargo Last-Mile Compliance	The system must enforce hazardous cargo transportation regulations for last-mile deliveries including IMDG class verification, driver ADR/hazmat certification validation, vehicle Tremcard availability, and route restrictions that avoid residential areas, tunnels, and bridges per local municipality regulations. For Qatar, the system must validate compliance with Qatar Civil Defence transport permits; for UAE, Abu Dhabi EHSMS and Dubai Municipality hazmat transport rules; for KSA, Saudi SFDA and Civil Defence requirements; for India, PESO and CPCB hazmat transport rules. Emergency response information must be accessible offline on the driver's mobile device. The system must block delivery dispatch if any compliance requirement is unmet and generate an exception for manual review.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R004	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement India DPDPA compliance by providing data principal rights (access, correction, erasure) for all Indian shipper and consignee personal data within statutory response timelines	System SHALL implement India DPDPA compliance by providing data principal rights (access, correction, erasure) for all Indian shipper and consignee personal data within statutory response timelines	must_have			"Indian data principals can submit access requests via self-service portal; system compiles all personal data within 72 hours; correction requests update records within 48 hours; erasure requests anonymize non-regulatory-required data within 30 days; request status is trackable by the data principal"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R005	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement automated data classification tagging for all shipping records, categorizing data as personal, sensitive-personal, business-confidential, or public based on content analysis at point of creation	System SHALL implement automated data classification tagging for all shipping records, categorizing data as personal, sensitive-personal, business-confidential, or public based on content analysis at point of creation	must_have			"All new records receive data classification tag at creation; personal data (names, contact info, passport numbers) is tagged automatically; sensitive personal data (financial details, biometrics for port access) receives elevated classification; classification tags are immutable and auditable; misclassification rate is below 1%"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R006	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL enforce cross-border data transfer controls requiring explicit approval workflow before transferring personal shipping data between Qatar, UAE, KSA, and India regions	System SHALL enforce cross-border data transfer controls requiring explicit approval workflow before transferring personal shipping data between Qatar, UAE, KSA, and India regions	must_have			"Cross-border transfer request initiates approval workflow with data protection officer; transfer is blocked until approved; approval records transfer purpose, legal basis, and data categories; unapproved transfer attempts are logged and alerted; emergency transfers for vessel safety have expedited 1-hour approval path"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R007	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement data masking for personal information when shipping records are accessed by users in jurisdictions without adequate data protection agreements, showing masked consignee names and contact details	System SHALL implement data masking for personal information when shipping records are accessed by users in jurisdictions without adequate data protection agreements, showing masked consignee names and contact details	must_have			"Users accessing from non-approved jurisdictions see masked personal data (e.g., 'J*** D**' for 'John Doe', '***@***.com' for emails); masking is applied at API gateway level before data leaves approved region; business-critical non-personal data (container numbers, port codes, vessel names) remains visible; masking rules are configurable per jurisdiction pair"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R008	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL maintain a data processing registry documenting all processing activities for personal data across shipping operations, including purpose, legal basis, retention period, and cross-border transfer status per jurisdiction	System SHALL maintain a data processing registry documenting all processing activities for personal data across shipping operations, including purpose, legal basis, retention period, and cross-border transfer status per jurisdiction	must_have			"Registry lists all personal data processing activities with purpose specification; legal basis is documented per jurisdiction (consent, contract, legal obligation); retention periods are defined per data category; registry is accessible to data protection officers; registry is updated within 5 business days of any processing change"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R009	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement data residency routing at the application layer, automatically directing database writes to the correct regional instance based on the nationality/jurisdiction of the data subject associated with the shipping transaction	System SHALL implement data residency routing at the application layer, automatically directing database writes to the correct regional instance based on the nationality/jurisdiction of the data subject associated with the shipping transaction	must_have			"Booking creation for Qatar-registered shipper routes write to Qatar database; UAE free zone operations route to UAE database; routing decision is logged with jurisdiction determination logic; misconfigured routing triggers immediate alert; routing rules support multi-jurisdiction shipments (e.g., Qatar shipper to India consignee) with data split across regions"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R010	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement right-to-erasure processing that anonymizes personal data in shipping records while preserving non-personal transaction data required for maritime regulatory retention (7-year BL retention, 5-year customs records)	System SHALL implement right-to-erasure processing that anonymizes personal data in shipping records while preserving non-personal transaction data required for maritime regulatory retention (7-year BL retention, 5-year customs records)	must_have			"Erasure request anonymizes personal fields (name, contact, ID numbers) while retaining container numbers, port codes, dates, and financial totals; anonymized records maintain referential integrity for regulatory reporting; BL records retain commercial terms for 7 years post-anonymization; audit trail of erasure action is maintained separately"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R011	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL generate data residency compliance reports per jurisdiction on monthly basis, documenting data volumes, transfer events, consent status, and any violations with remediation actions	System SHALL generate data residency compliance reports per jurisdiction on monthly basis, documenting data volumes, transfer events, consent status, and any violations with remediation actions	must_have			"Monthly report per jurisdiction shows total personal data records stored; cross-border transfers are itemized with approval status; consent withdrawal count and processing impact are documented; any residency violations are listed with root cause and remediation; report is generated automatically by 5th business day of following month"	pending
FEAT-026-2-001-R012	FEAT-026-2-001	MOD-026	Multi-Drop Delivery Route Planning	The system must support multi-drop delivery routes where a single truck delivers multiple containers or LCL consignments to different consignees in a single trip. The route planner must optimize the delivery sequence to minimize total travel distance and time while respecting each consignee's delivery window constraints, truck maximum payload limits, and local traffic restriction zones (e.g., Dubai truck ban hours 6:30-8:30 AM and 1:00-3:30 PM on Sheikh Zayed Road). The system must display the optimized route on a map with turn-by-turn navigation data exportable to the driver's mobile device. Route replanning must trigger automatically when a delivery exception occurs at any stop along the multi-drop route.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R013	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement data localization for shipping document attachments (scanned BLs, customs forms, packing lists) storing binary files in the same jurisdiction as the associated transaction metadata	System SHALL implement data localization for shipping document attachments (scanned BLs, customs forms, packing lists) storing binary files in the same jurisdiction as the associated transaction metadata	must_have			"Document uploads for Qatar transactions store in Qatar-region object storage; UAE documents in UAE storage; document download requests are served from local region; CDN caching does not replicate documents to non-compliant regions; storage location is verifiable via metadata query"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R014	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL support data residency requirements for multi-leg shipments (e.g., transshipment via UAE from India to Qatar) by splitting and storing jurisdiction-specific data segments in respective regional databases	System SHALL support data residency requirements for multi-leg shipments (e.g., transshipment via UAE from India to Qatar) by splitting and storing jurisdiction-specific data segments in respective regional databases	should_have			"Transshipment booking with India origin, UAE transshipment, and Qatar destination stores Indian shipper data in India, UAE port operations data in UAE, and Qatar consignee data in Qatar; unified shipment view reconstructs data from all regions with appropriate access controls; cross-region query completes within 5 seconds"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R015	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement automated data breach notification workflows per jurisdiction, notifying Qatar NCDP within 72 hours, UAE DPO within 72 hours, KSA NDMO within 72 hours, and India DPB within 72 hours of confirmed personal data breach detection	System SHALL implement automated data breach notification workflows per jurisdiction, notifying Qatar NCDP within 72 hours, UAE DPO within 72 hours, KSA NDMO within 72 hours, and India DPB within 72 hours of confirmed personal data breach detection	must_have			"Breach detection triggers jurisdiction-specific notification workflow; notification template includes breach scope, affected data subjects count, remediation steps per regulatory requirement; workflow tracks notification submission and acknowledgment; notifications are sent in Arabic (Qatar, UAE, KSA) and English (India); notification deadline countdown is visible on incident dashboard"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R016	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement privacy impact assessment (PIA) workflow that must be completed before any new shipping data processing activity is deployed, with approval gates from jurisdiction-specific data protection officers	System SHALL implement privacy impact assessment (PIA) workflow that must be completed before any new shipping data processing activity is deployed, with approval gates from jurisdiction-specific data protection officers	should_have			"New data processing features cannot be deployed without completed PIA; PIA template covers data categories, processing purpose, risk assessment, and mitigation measures; jurisdiction-specific DPO approval is required for each affected region; PIA records are retained for the lifetime of the processing activity plus 3 years"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R017	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement audit logging of all personal data access events with immutable records capturing accessor identity, data subject jurisdiction, data categories accessed, purpose, and timestamp for regulatory investigation support	System SHALL implement audit logging of all personal data access events with immutable records capturing accessor identity, data subject jurisdiction, data categories accessed, purpose, and timestamp for regulatory investigation support	must_have			"Every read/write of personal data generates audit log entry; log includes accessor user ID, role, IP, jurisdiction, data subject ID, data categories, and stated purpose; audit logs are immutable and tamper-evident; logs are retained for 5 years; regulatory investigators can query audit logs by data subject ID across all jurisdictions within 30 seconds"	pending
FEAT-002-2-004-R018	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL provide a data sovereignty configuration interface allowing system administrators to define and update jurisdiction-to-region mappings, data classification rules, and cross-border transfer policies without code deployment	System SHALL provide a data sovereignty configuration interface allowing system administrators to define and update jurisdiction-to-region mappings, data classification rules, and cross-border transfer policies without code deployment	should_have			"Admin interface allows adding new jurisdiction with associated region, classification rules, and transfer policies; changes take effect within 5 minutes without service restart; configuration changes are version-controlled with rollback capability; changes require dual-approval from compliance and engineering leads; audit trail captures all configuration modifications"	pending
FEAT-002-3-001-R001	FEAT-002-3-001	MOD-002	Zero Trust Policy Engine	Implement a centralized zero trust policy engine that enforces deny-by-default access control for all microservice-to-microservice communication, requiring explicit identity verification and authorization for every request regardless of network origin	must_have	AI agent continuously analyzes service communication patterns to auto-generate least-privilege policies, detecting anomalous traffic flows and recommending policy tightening or alerting on zero-trust violations in real time	Security architect reviews and approves AI-generated zero trust policies before enforcement, validates exception requests from development teams, and conducts quarterly policy audits	["All inter-service calls are denied by default until explicitly whitelisted in policy engine", "Policy engine evaluates identity, device posture, and request context for every API call", "Policy changes propagate to all service meshes within 30 seconds", "Unauthorized access attempts are logged with full context and trigger real-time alerts", "System maintains 99.99% uptime for policy evaluation with sub-5ms latency overhead"]	pending
FEAT-026-2-001-R013	FEAT-026-2-001	MOD-026	Delivery Document Generation in Bilingual Format	The system must generate all last-mile delivery documents in bilingual Arabic/English format on a single document. Required documents include the Delivery Note, Gate Pass, Driver Manifest, and Vehicle Loading Plan. Each document must include the entity's legal name in Arabic and English, commercial registration number, VAT/tax identification number, and QR code linking to the digital verification page. The Delivery Note must list container numbers, seal numbers, package count, gross weight in kilograms, and cargo description in both languages. All documents must be printable in A4 format and available as digitally signed PDFs conforming to the ZUGFeRD or UAE-mandated PEPPOL e-invoicing standards where applicable.	must_have			[]	pending
