FEAT-026-2-002-R010	FEAT-026-2-002	MOD-026	MBL Surrender and Release Workflow	The system must manage the surrender of original Multimodal Bills of Lading at destination and the release workflow for cargo delivery. For original BL terms, the system must track the number of originals outstanding and block cargo release until at least one original is surrendered and verified. For Sea Waybill terms, cargo may be released upon vessel arrival without document surrender. For Telex Release, the system must record the origin office's telex release instruction with authorization reference before permitting destination release. The release workflow must generate a Delivery Order to the port/ICD terminal referencing the MBL number, container details, and consignee identity. Multi-entity scenarios where the BL is issued by the Qatar entity but cargo is released at a KSA ICD must be handled via inter-entity release authorization with dual-entity audit logging.	must_have			[]	pending
