FEAT-002-2-004-R012	FEAT-002-2-004	MOD-002	System SHALL implement encryption key sovereignty ensuring that encryption keys for each jurisdiction's data are managed within that jurisdiction's region and are not accessible from other regions	System SHALL implement encryption key sovereignty ensuring that encryption keys for each jurisdiction's data are managed within that jurisdiction's region and are not accessible from other regions	must_have			"Qatar data encryption keys are stored and managed exclusively in Qatar-region KMS; UAE keys in UAE-region KMS; KSA and India keys similarly isolated; key access audit shows no cross-region key retrieval; key rotation occurs independently per region every 90 days; compromised key in one region does not affect other regions"	pending
FEAT-002-3-001-R002	FEAT-002-3-001	MOD-002	Mutual TLS Service Mesh	Deploy a service mesh with mandatory mutual TLS (mTLS) for all microservice communication, ensuring encrypted and authenticated traffic between every service pair with automatic certificate provisioning via SPIFFE/SPIRE identity framework	must_have	AI agent monitors mTLS handshake metrics and certificate health across the mesh, predicting certificate expiration risks and automatically flagging services with weak cipher suites or misconfigured TLS settings	Infrastructure team approves service mesh configuration changes, reviews mTLS exception requests for legacy integrations, and validates cipher suite policy updates	["100% of inter-service traffic is encrypted with mTLS using TLS 1.3 minimum", "Each service receives a unique SPIFFE identity with automatic certificate provisioning", "mTLS handshake adds no more than 2ms latency to service-to-service calls", "Services without valid certificates are automatically rejected from the mesh", "Certificate rotation occurs automatically every 24 hours without service disruption"]	pending
FEAT-002-3-001-R008	FEAT-002-3-001	MOD-002	Automated Certificate Lifecycle Management	Implement end-to-end certificate lifecycle management covering issuance, renewal, rotation, and revocation for all TLS certificates across public endpoints, internal services, and API gateways with zero-downtime rotation and expiry alerting	must_have	AI agent tracks all certificate expiration dates across the platform, initiating automatic renewal 30 days before expiry, predicting certificate chain issues, and alerting on certificates using deprecated algorithms or short key lengths	Security team approves new root and intermediate CA certificates, reviews certificate policy exceptions, and manages relationships with external certificate authorities	["All certificates are automatically renewed at least 30 days before expiration", "Certificate rotation completes with zero downtime using graceful rollover", "System maintains a complete inventory of all active certificates with expiry tracking", "Revoked certificates are propagated to all services via CRL/OCSP within 15 minutes", "Alerts fire at 30-day, 14-day, and 7-day thresholds for any certificate approaching expiry"]	pending
FEAT-002-3-001-R014	FEAT-002-3-001	MOD-002	Third-Party Integration Network Controls	Implement dedicated network controls for third-party integrations including port authority systems, customs APIs, shipping line partners, and banking/payment gateways, enforcing strict allow-listing, traffic inspection, and rate limiting per partner connection	must_have	AI agent monitors third-party integration traffic for unusual patterns such as unexpected data volumes, off-hours access, or protocol deviations, scoring each integration partner's risk level and recommending access restriction adjustments	Integration team onboards new third-party connections through a security review process, compliance officer approves partner access levels, and security team investigates anomalous partner traffic alerts	["Each third-party integration connects through a dedicated gateway with IP allow-listing", "All partner traffic is inspected for payload compliance and protocol adherence", "Rate limits are enforced per partner with configurable thresholds per integration type", "Partner access can be revoked within 5 minutes in case of security incident", "Monthly partner access reports show traffic volumes, error rates, and security events per integration"]	pending
FEAT-002-3-002-R005	FEAT-002-3-002	MOD-002	Backup Integrity Verification and Testing	Implement automated backup integrity verification through regular restore testing, checksum validation, and data consistency checks ensuring that every backup can be successfully restored when needed for disaster recovery	must_have	AI agent schedules and executes automated restore tests on a rotating basis, comparing restored data against source checksums, detecting corruption patterns, and predicting backup reliability scores based on historical verification results	DBA team reviews weekly backup verification reports, investigates any failed restore tests, and certifies backup recoverability for quarterly DR audits	["Every backup undergoes automated checksum verification within 2 hours of completion", "Automated restore testing runs weekly for critical databases with full data consistency validation", "Restore test results are logged with duration, data integrity score, and any discrepancies found", "Failed integrity checks trigger immediate re-backup and alert to DBA team", "Monthly backup recoverability report shows 100% successful restore rate for all critical databases"]	pending
FEAT-002-3-002-R011	FEAT-002-3-002	MOD-002	Backup Monitoring and Alerting Dashboard	Deploy a centralized backup monitoring dashboard providing real-time visibility into backup job status, storage utilization, replication health, retention compliance, and recovery readiness across all databases and regions	should_have	AI agent analyzes backup metrics trends to predict storage capacity needs, forecast backup window overruns, and identify databases with degrading backup performance before they impact recovery objectives	Operations team monitors dashboard during daily standup, DBA team investigates backup health alerts, and management reviews weekly backup health summary reports	["Dashboard displays real-time status of all backup jobs across regions with success/failure indicators", "Storage utilization is tracked per database and region with 30-day growth projections", "Alerts fire within 5 minutes of backup job failure, replication lag exceeding threshold, or storage capacity warnings", "Dashboard includes backup SLA compliance metrics showing RPO/RTO achievement rates", "Historical backup metrics are retained for 12 months enabling trend analysis and capacity planning"]	pending
FEAT-006-1-001-R001	FEAT-006-1-001	MOD-006	Multi-Lane Booking Creation	Customers create new container shipping bookings by selecting origin/destination ports across Qatar (Hamad Port), Dubai (Jebel Ali), KSA (Jeddah Islamic Port, King Abdulaziz Port), and Indian ports (Nhava Sheva, Mundra, Chennai).	must_have			["System displays all active port pairs with estimated transit times for Qatar-Dubai, Qatar-KSA, Qatar-India, Dubai-KSA, Dubai-India, and KSA-India routes", "Customer selects origin port, destination port, and requested ETD within a 30-day forward window", "Booking form validates that selected port pair has at least one active vessel service before submission", "System rejects bookings for embargoed or sanctioned port pairs and displays regulatory reason in English and Arabic"]	pending
FEAT-006-1-001-R003	FEAT-006-1-001	MOD-006	AI-Driven Rate Quotation	AI engine generates instant freight rate quotations based on route, container type, commodity, and customer contract tier without requiring manual sales approval for standard bookings.	must_have			["AI returns a freight rate quote within 3 seconds of booking parameter submission for standard commodity codes", "Rate quote displays base ocean freight, BAF, CAF, THC at origin, THC at destination, and any applicable surcharges as separate line items", "Rates are displayed in customer's preferred currency (QAR, AED, SAR, INR, USD) with live FX conversion from base USD rate", "Quotes for hazardous (IMO class 1-9) or out-of-gauge cargo are flagged for manual pricing review with estimated response SLA of 4 hours"]	pending
FEAT-026-2-003-R004	FEAT-026-2-003	MOD-026	Distance-Based and Zone-Based Rating Models	The system must support both distance-based and zone-based rating models for inland haulage. Distance-based rating must calculate charges using a per-kilometer rate multiplied by the route distance sourced from an integrated mapping provider, with minimum charge thresholds per container type. Zone-based rating must assign origin and destination locations to predefined geographic zones with rates defined per zone pair. The zone master must be configurable per entity: Qatar zones by municipality, UAE zones by emirate and industrial area, KSA zones by administrative region and major city clusters, India zones by state and district. Hybrid models combining a zone-based base rate with distance-based increments beyond zone boundaries must also be supported. The system must display the applicable rating model and calculation breakdown on every rate quotation and invoice.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-026-2-003-R010	FEAT-026-2-003	MOD-026	Fuel Surcharge Index Management	The system must manage fuel surcharge indices linked to local diesel price benchmarks for each operating jurisdiction. Fuel price sources must be configurable: Qatar Woqod published prices, UAE ENOC/ADNOC monthly prices, KSA Saudi Aramco domestic diesel prices, and India Indian Oil Corporation diesel prices by city. The system must automatically retrieve or allow manual entry of fuel prices on a defined schedule (weekly, bi-weekly, or monthly). Fuel surcharge calculations must apply a predefined formula per rate card: typically a base fuel price (frozen at contract inception) with surcharge percentage adjusting proportionally to the current price delta. The system must maintain a historical fuel price database for audit and dispute resolution. When fuel surcharges change, the system must notify affected customers and haulers with the new rate effective date, calculated in the entity's base currency.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-026-2-003-R012	FEAT-026-2-003	MOD-026	Demurrage and Detention Rate Management for Inland	The system must manage inland demurrage and detention rate schedules separate from port/shipping line tariffs. Inland detention covers the use of containers beyond free time at customer premises, while inland demurrage covers storage of laden containers at ICDs beyond free time. Free time rules must be configurable per ICD, container type, and customer agreement: standard free time for import containers at Indian ICDs is typically 3 days, at GCC ICDs typically 5 days. Rates must escalate in configurable time slabs (e.g., days 1-5 at rate X, days 6-10 at rate Y, days 11+ at rate Z). The system must automatically calculate charges daily, generate invoices at configurable intervals, and support dispute workflows where customers contest charges. All charges must be in the ICD location's entity currency with detailed day-by-day calculation breakdowns available.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-026-2-003-R014	FEAT-026-2-003	MOD-026	Rate Audit Trail and Approval Workflow	The system must enforce an approval workflow for all rate card creation, modification, and deletion operations. Rate changes must pass through a configurable approval chain: rate analyst creates or modifies the rate, pricing manager reviews and approves, and finance controller provides final sign-off for rates exceeding a configurable value threshold. The approval workflow must support delegation rules for approver absence. Every rate change must generate an immutable audit trail recording the previous value, new value, change reason, requester identity, approver identities, timestamps, and IP addresses. Bulk rate changes (e.g., annual escalation affecting hundreds of rate lines) must be submitted as a single change request with consolidated approval. The audit trail must be searchable by rate card, date range, user, and change type, with export capabilities in Arabic and English.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-026-2-003-R016	FEAT-026-2-003	MOD-026	Historical Rate Analysis and Trend Reporting	The system must provide historical rate analysis tools showing inland haulage rate trends over configurable time periods (3 months, 6 months, 12 months, 24 months). Analysis must be available per route, container type, transport mode, and hauler. Trend charts must display average rate per TEU, rate distribution (min/max/median), fuel surcharge component trend, and total cost trend including all surcharges. Comparison views must allow benchmarking of a specific hauler's rates against market average for the same route. Forecasting tools must use historical trend data to project rate movements for budget planning, using linear regression or weighted moving average methods selectable by the user. All monetary values must be normalizable to a common currency for cross-entity comparison. Reports must be exportable in PDF and Excel with Arabic RTL support and Hijri date formatting options.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-026-2-004-R002	FEAT-026-2-004	MOD-026	Real-Time Capacity and Availability Integration	The optimization engine must incorporate real-time capacity and availability data from connected transport providers. This includes vessel space availability from ocean carrier booking systems, rail wagon availability from railway operators (CONCOR for India, SAR for KSA), truck and chassis availability from contracted haulers, ICD yard capacity and congestion levels, and port terminal berth and gate congestion data from Hamad Port (QAHMD), Jebel Ali (AEJEA), Khalifa Port (AEKHL), and JNPT (INJNP). When capacity data is unavailable due to API downtime or connectivity issues, the system must fall back to statistical capacity estimates based on historical utilization patterns for the same day of week and season. Capacity data freshness must be displayed on the optimization results with staleness warnings when data exceeds 4 hours.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-026-2-004-R004	FEAT-026-2-004	MOD-026	Dynamic Re-Routing for Disruption Response	The system must automatically detect transport disruptions and propose alternative routes in near-real-time. Disruption triggers must include vessel schedule delays exceeding 24 hours, port closures or severe congestion alerts (e.g., Jebel Ali gate queue exceeding 4 hours), rail service cancellations, road closures due to weather or accidents, customs holds or regulatory inspections causing delays, and labour actions affecting terminals or haulers. Upon detecting a disruption, the AI engine must re-optimize affected shipments considering current positions and committed delivery dates, ranking alternatives by cost impact and delivery date deviation. Re-routing proposals must be presented to dispatchers with one-click acceptance or manual modification capability. The system must calculate the cost differential between original and re-routed plans in the booking currency and flag any contractual SLA impacts.	must_have			[]	pending
FEAT-006-1-001-R015	FEAT-006-1-001	MOD-006	Multi-Currency Rate Lock	Customers lock the quoted freight rate in their preferred currency for a configurable validity period to hedge against FX fluctuations.	must_have			["Rate lock is offered in QAR, AED, SAR, INR, and USD with validity period configurable per entity (default 48 hours)", "Locked rate is guaranteed regardless of FX movement during the validity window; FX gain/loss is absorbed by the operating entity", "System displays countdown timer showing remaining rate lock validity on the booking confirmation screen", "Expired rate locks trigger automatic re-quotation at current rates with customer notification before booking proceeds"]	pending
