FEAT-006-1-002-R009	FEAT-006-1-002	MOD-006	Tracking Data API for Customer Integration	RESTful API enables customers to integrate shipment tracking data into their own ERP/WMS systems programmatically.	must_have			["API provides endpoints for: list shipments, get shipment detail, get milestones, get ETA, and subscribe to webhooks", "API authenticates via OAuth 2.0 client credentials with customer-specific API keys and rate limiting (100 requests/minute)", "Webhook subscriptions push milestone and exception events to customer-configured HTTPS endpoints with HMAC-SHA256 signature verification", "API documentation is available in OpenAPI 3.0 format with interactive Swagger UI accessible from the portal"]	pending
FEAT-006-1-003-R002	FEAT-006-1-003	MOD-006	Shipping Instruction Submission	Customers submit Shipping Instructions (SI) through structured forms with AI validation against booking data.	must_have			["SI form captures: shipper, consignee, notify party, marks/numbers, goods description, HS code, weight, measurement, and special instructions", "AI validates SI data against original booking: container count, weight, commodity code, and flags mismatches for customer correction", "SI submission deadline is enforced based on vessel cut-off (configurable per trade lane, default 3 days before ETD) with countdown displayed", "Late SI submissions incur an automatic late documentation fee added to the customer's invoice per entity tariff schedule"]	pending
FEAT-006-1-004-R005	FEAT-006-1-004	MOD-006	Partial Payment and Payment Allocation	Customers make partial payments against invoices and allocate payments across multiple invoices.	must_have			["Customer can pay any amount between the minimum partial payment threshold (configurable per entity, default 10% of invoice) and full invoice amount", "Multi-invoice payment allows customer to select multiple open invoices and pay them in a single transaction with automatic allocation", "When partial payment is made, system updates invoice status to 'Partially Paid' and shows remaining balance", "Payment allocation follows customer's explicit selection; if not specified, system applies FIFO (oldest invoice first) by default"]	pending
FEAT-006-1-004-R007	FEAT-006-1-004	MOD-006	Invoice Dispute Management	Customers raise and track invoice disputes through a structured workflow with document upload and communication thread.	must_have			["Customer selects specific line items on an invoice to dispute with mandatory reason code (overcharge, service not rendered, incorrect rate, duplicate charge) and free-text explanation", "Disputed line items are flagged in the system; disputed amount is excluded from aging and late payment penalty calculations during investigation", "Dispute communication thread allows back-and-forth messages between customer and finance team with document attachments", "Dispute resolution SLA is displayed (configurable per entity, default 10 business days) with escalation path if SLA is breached"]	pending
